# Mutation plan for the four team writes.
#
#   scripts/mutate-batch.sh scripts/mutations/team-writes.plan
#
# The decisions here are unusually easy to "tidy" into something wrong:
#
#   * `UpdateOptions{Sanitized: true}` copies **seven** fields onto the stored team and discards
#     the rest of the body — a port that wrote the submitted struct would let a client change a
#     team's type or un-archive it through an ordinary update;
#   * the name is taken only when non-empty, changed, **and not `-`**;
#   * turning `AllowOpenInvite` off mints a new invite id, which nothing in the request names;
#   * the two routes decide the conditional `invite_user` permission differently — by *change* on
#     update, by *presence* on patch;
#   * the websocket event is sanitised and the HTTP answer is not.
#
# **Three mutations are deliberately not here, because they are equivalent mutants.** Measured —
# each survives, and none is a gap in the tests:
#
#   * `team.create_at = old.create_at` in the store. Every caller passes a team it has just
#     *fetched*, so the value is already the stored one and the assignment cannot change anything.
#     Go carries the same redundancy.
#   * `team.update_at = get_millis()` in the store, for the same reason: `write_team` has already
#     called `pre_update`, which sets it. Go calls `PreUpdate` and then assigns again too.
#   * swapping `invalid_param("id")` for `invalid_param("team_id")`. `AppError.Params` is
#     `json:"-"`, so the parameter name never reaches the client on either server — the id and the
#     status are identical either way.
#
# The last two lines are the no-op controls and must SURVIVE.
team-update-writes-the-submitted-type	crates/mm-app/src/team.rs	        old_team.display_name = team.display_name.clone();	        old_team.team_type = team.team_type.clone();\n        old_team.display_name = team.display_name.clone();	api	team_writes
team-update-writes-the-submitted-delete-at	crates/mm-app/src/team.rs	        old_team.description = team.description.clone();	        old_team.delete_at = team.delete_at;\n        old_team.description = team.description.clone();	api	team_writes
team-update-writes-the-submitted-invite-id	crates/mm-app/src/team.rs	        old_team.company_name = team.company_name.clone();	        old_team.invite_id = team.invite_id.clone();\n        old_team.company_name = team.company_name.clone();	api	team_writes
team-update-drops-the-display-name	crates/mm-app/src/team.rs	        old_team.display_name = team.display_name.clone();	        // the display name is not copied	api	team_writes
